target:    .github/workflows/ci.yml
gate:      php tests/ci-matrix-coverage-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    PHP 7.4
rationale: The coupling this commit created, read from the other end. PHP 7.4 has no PHPUnit lane and no static-only exemption -- the 6.4 E2E include pair is the only thing in CI that loads the plugin on it, which is why the pair-aware scan was added in the first place. Dropping 6.4 from the blocking list leaves that pair in the matrix and still running, so nothing about the matrix looks different; what changes is that its verdict is thrown away again, exactly as in run 33771753689. Before the credit became conditional this edit was invisible to every gate in the repo. Now it costs 7.4 its only execution coverage and the failure names the version, not the workflow line.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@
         # everything, dropping either version, or reverting to a bare `true` all
         # fail that gate. §7 used to match only the literal `continue-on-error:
         # true`, so before this commit it would have matched nothing here.
-        continue-on-error: ${{ !contains(fromJSON('["6.4","7.1"]'), matrix.wp) }}
+        continue-on-error: ${{ !contains(fromJSON('["7.1"]'), matrix.wp) }}
         env:
           # wp-env creates a fresh WordPress with default admin credentials.
           # Override WP_ADMIN_USER / WP_ADMIN_PASS in global-setup.ts.
